he staff beamed to A5. That is bar 93. Next bar: a grace-note mark under a slur, G5, an 8th rest, then C5. That is bar 94. The next bar holds beamed 8th double stops in two voices. That is bar 95. Then a C5 with a slur, a 32nd group falling to a dotted F4, an 8th rest and C5. That is bar 96. After the next barline the double-stop 8ths repeat, which is bar 97. A last short stretch begins about x≈1365: a C5 under the same arc as in bar 96, a 32nd group falling to a dotted F4, then one 8th near the end of the staff. That is bar 98: C5, A4 G4 F4., C5. The line may stop partway through bar 98, with the final F4 on the next line. The program's last bar, 97, ends too early. One stretch is unclear: before bar 93 I count about 7 noteheads where bars 91–92 need 6. The two G5s look like separate tied notes, which may explain it. Even so, the start fits bar 91 better than bar 90, because the first beamed pair is A5/F#5, not Bb5/G#5.","right":false,"insights":"The double stops in bars 95–98 make the end easy to place. The repeat of the bar 96 figure (quarter, 32nds, dotted F4) after bar 97 shows the line runs into bar 98. The opening is harder: ties are written as separate noteheads, ledger lines are faint and the barlines in the first third are hard to see. A sharper scan of the first 300 px, or marked barline positions, would settle the opening note count."},"ttft_ms":36105,"type":"result","duration_ms":44488,"uuid":"14b6a35f-9dfd-4568-85cc-7e7fdfb7d47d","ttft_stream_ms":1419,"time_to_request_ms":340,"first_content_frame_ms":1419,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":3918,"cacheReadInputTokens":523,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5307,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12092859999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3138,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":5307,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","cos